{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke to me.</b> Rashi explained: but from the sending of the spies until here it does not say וידבר but only ויאמר, to teach you that all thirty-eight years that Israel were rebuked, the dibbur was not singled out with him, etc. The meaning: דבור implies from His mouth many things, and it is an expression of affection, like two lovers who speak with one another out of affection. But אמירה implies a paucity of words — mere saying, nothing more. And in Ta'anit, Rashi explained: the dibbur was not in distinctness and affection, as it is written וידבר HaShem אלי — the dibbur was singled out with me; and even though before this there are verses in which וידבר is written, some say: the dibbur was not to Moses mouth to mouth, but in a night vision."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:25.216683170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}